WEBVTT

00:21.291 --> 00:24.581
TROLL

00:24.751 --> 00:26.921
There are no major changes.

00:27.251 --> 00:29.671
You will be compensated
with five pounds of gold.

00:29.751 --> 00:32.341
I will only pay you in exchange for his dead body.

00:34.881 --> 00:38.011
You can do whatever you want with their ship
and their cargo.

00:39.561 --> 00:41.221
Kill Thors.

00:42.891 --> 00:45.901
-Go ahead, boy.
-My turn next.

00:45.981 --> 00:47.561
Thors?

00:48.271 --> 00:50.231
The Troll of Jom.

00:50.321 --> 00:51.981
I've heard of him before.

00:52.071 --> 00:55.701
Are you sure it's okay if I kill him?
He's a hero to you guys.

00:57.531 --> 01:00.031
If he were a hero, I wouldn't have told you to kill him.

01:00.121 --> 01:02.831
He broke military law.

01:02.911 --> 01:04.461
He deserted during battle.

01:04.541 --> 01:08.171
Orders to have him executed were issued
15 years ago.

01:10.381 --> 01:15.341
I know you have strict laws,
but it's been 15 years.

01:17.221 --> 01:18.301
Thanks.

01:22.261 --> 01:23.811
No, don't get the wrong idea.

01:23.891 --> 01:27.231
As long as I receive fair payment,

01:27.311 --> 01:28.771
I'll do any job.

01:28.851 --> 01:31.021
But you know, master...

01:31.111 --> 01:35.651
If you're going to execute one of your own,
one of your own should kill him.

01:36.701 --> 01:39.071
You went to Iceland, right?

01:39.571 --> 01:41.871
Why didn't you kill him there?

01:43.791 --> 01:46.001
This Christian monk is dead.

01:47.081 --> 01:49.581
It's none of your business.

01:50.001 --> 01:53.211
You shouldn't ask questions.
It's for your own good.

01:55.591 --> 01:57.131
Well, all right.

01:57.511 --> 01:59.801
Five extra pounds of gold, paid in advance.

01:59.891 --> 02:01.221
Then I'll accept your job.

02:06.681 --> 02:11.191
You think you have the upper hand on me.
You must be confident in yourself.

02:21.321 --> 02:23.371
Oops, sorry.

02:23.911 --> 02:27.201
It slipped. Are you okay?

02:27.291 --> 02:29.501
Hey. Be careful.

02:29.581 --> 02:32.001
You guys almost hit me.

02:32.081 --> 02:33.211
You klutz.

02:33.291 --> 02:35.001
You drank too much.

02:36.261 --> 02:39.131
Five extra pounds of gold, paid in advance.

02:39.551 --> 02:41.341
You accept?

02:46.181 --> 02:47.351
All right.

02:49.641 --> 02:53.611
Excellent, master.
You're a great man. See you later.

02:54.821 --> 02:56.481
And by the way...

02:57.401 --> 03:00.491
What kind of a warrior is Thors?

03:00.571 --> 03:03.531
What does he look like? How does he fight?

03:06.291 --> 03:09.751
Thors is no longer a warrior.

03:14.461 --> 03:16.631
Okay. That's enough drinking.

03:16.711 --> 03:19.381
It's time to work, you bastards.

03:19.971 --> 03:22.181
Bjorn. Nice spear throw.

03:22.261 --> 03:23.261
No sweat.

03:23.721 --> 03:26.391
Even Floki was in shock.

03:26.471 --> 03:28.561
I wish I could have seen it myself.

03:34.981 --> 03:37.321
It seems he's not a man of empty words.

05:16.041 --> 05:20.001
The time has come for me,
Ari, son of Geitr, to become a man.

05:20.461 --> 05:24.381
I know. Don't say a word.
It will not be an easy journey.

05:25.051 --> 05:28.761
There's no guarantee that I won't be injured in battle.

05:29.091 --> 05:31.101
But I shall return.

05:31.181 --> 05:35.981
I'll return with a necklace
I seized from England as a gift to you.

05:36.061 --> 05:38.731
-And then will you...?
-Hey, I'm still sleepy.

05:39.311 --> 05:41.611
Ma-- Marry...

05:41.691 --> 05:42.731
Ari.

05:43.481 --> 05:46.741
You forgot your lunch.

05:46.821 --> 05:47.651
Mom?

05:47.741 --> 05:50.991
Why are you so careless?

05:51.081 --> 05:53.911
Make sure you share the salted herring
with everyone else.

05:53.991 --> 05:55.871
-I stuffed it full.
-Mom. Wait over there.

05:55.951 --> 05:58.331
How can you say that to your own mother?

05:58.421 --> 06:00.001
-When I return...
-What's wrong...?

06:00.081 --> 06:02.131
I'll finish what I was saying.
Wait for me, Ylva.

06:09.051 --> 06:12.011
They're departing today.

06:12.681 --> 06:14.971
I hope they don't die.

06:15.351 --> 06:16.521
Ylva.

06:16.601 --> 06:18.351
Do you have a moment?

06:18.441 --> 06:19.811
Wait. I'm first.

06:19.901 --> 06:21.611
Hey. Ylva.

06:22.021 --> 06:23.521
Can you try somewhere else?

06:29.031 --> 06:32.371
Make sure you bathe on Saturday, my boy.

06:32.451 --> 06:33.661
I know, Mom.

06:34.031 --> 06:35.491
I swear on my father's ax.

06:35.581 --> 06:38.251
I shall bring back a barrel full of gold coins.

06:39.121 --> 06:41.671
They're so excited.

06:41.751 --> 06:45.461
But there's only five of them in total.
That's not enough.

06:45.551 --> 06:48.131
Thors says that five is enough.

06:49.471 --> 06:52.011
Well, if that's what he says.

06:52.091 --> 06:56.851
But that's barely enough
for sailing two ships.

06:56.931 --> 07:00.941
It's Thors we're talking about.
I'm sure he has a reason.

07:01.601 --> 07:04.691
Hey. What were you talking about with Ylva just now?

07:04.771 --> 07:07.691
Shut up, you jackass. You stay away from her.

07:08.361 --> 07:10.781
Watch your back on the battlefield.

07:10.861 --> 07:13.571
Don't underestimate me.
I was going to say the same thing to you.

07:14.031 --> 07:15.781
-Ari.
-What?

07:20.001 --> 07:21.291
Be careful.

07:24.381 --> 07:25.881
You didn't finish.

07:25.961 --> 07:27.251
What did you say?

07:27.341 --> 07:29.171
This way.

07:29.801 --> 07:30.801
Miss.

07:32.131 --> 07:33.681
Are you worried about Ari?

07:34.511 --> 07:37.681
Want me to tell you a secret?

07:39.271 --> 07:41.691
What? They're not going to battle?

07:43.231 --> 07:44.561
It's a secret.

07:45.361 --> 07:49.111
We're going to stop by Norway
on our way to Jomsborg.

07:49.191 --> 07:53.701
Thors plans to leave the young men behind there.

07:54.281 --> 07:58.741
Thors is going to get some help
from some sailors in Norway

07:58.831 --> 08:00.581
to make it to Jomsborg.

08:00.911 --> 08:04.711
I'm friends with the previous King of Norway.

08:04.921 --> 08:06.711
I have a lot of influence there.

08:07.041 --> 08:10.171
As soon as I'm done with my business,

08:10.261 --> 08:12.341
I'll bring the young men back here.

08:14.181 --> 08:18.351
Five men is the most I can bring back
on my run-down ship.

08:19.061 --> 08:22.521
He won't bring anyone to the battlefield.

08:23.851 --> 08:26.731
That's the kind of person that Thors is.

08:31.241 --> 08:32.241
Thorfinn.

08:33.571 --> 08:35.911
Hey. Where are you?

08:36.451 --> 08:38.081
Thorfinn.

08:42.911 --> 08:44.671
Excuse me, Leif...

08:45.711 --> 08:50.421
Does that mean Thors is going
to the battlefield alone?

08:54.721 --> 08:56.641
Ready to row?

08:57.181 --> 08:58.471
Yeah.

09:05.851 --> 09:07.771
What's wrong with his oar?

09:08.231 --> 09:12.071
I can't believe Thorfinn isn't seeing Father off.

09:12.571 --> 09:15.531
I bet he's still angry he got scolded yesterday.

09:16.071 --> 09:17.781
-Helga.
-Yes?

09:18.871 --> 09:20.411
Tell Thorfinn...

09:22.621 --> 09:23.621
Well...

09:25.291 --> 09:26.291
What I mean is...

09:29.331 --> 09:31.671
Yes. I'll tell him.

09:35.301 --> 09:36.171
I'm counting on you.

09:38.301 --> 09:40.681
All right. Depart.

09:52.651 --> 09:53.781
He's so strong.

09:53.861 --> 09:55.491
Idiot. Don't stop rowing.

09:55.901 --> 09:57.111
Row. Row.

10:02.081 --> 10:04.491
You can do it.

10:04.581 --> 10:07.001
Bring home some souvenirs.

10:07.081 --> 10:09.711
See you.

10:13.591 --> 10:15.671
Raise the sail.

10:25.971 --> 10:27.431
My hands are peeling.

10:27.521 --> 10:29.061
My butt. My butt.

10:30.601 --> 10:32.061
Hey. Hang in there.

10:33.151 --> 10:34.731
Ari. Take the rudder.

10:36.031 --> 10:40.321
Mord and Magni, adjust the mainsheet.
Hakon and Grim, take the jib sheet.

10:41.821 --> 10:42.991
Are you tired?

10:44.031 --> 10:46.161
No. It's nothing.

10:48.751 --> 10:51.671
Don't worry.
We don't have to row any more for a while.

10:52.331 --> 10:55.631
We're riding the current now.
The ship will move on its own.

10:55.711 --> 10:59.011
Does that mean we can't turn back anymore, Father?

10:59.091 --> 11:00.511
Yeah, that's right.

11:02.141 --> 11:02.971
"Father"?

11:07.271 --> 11:08.271
Thor--?

11:08.351 --> 11:09.851
Thorfinn? You...

11:09.941 --> 11:11.271
You can tell me later.

11:16.021 --> 11:17.941
I made it...

11:30.001 --> 11:31.831
You naughty--

11:31.921 --> 11:32.921
Father.

11:34.171 --> 11:35.171
It's the ocean.

11:49.021 --> 11:51.691
This job is suspicious.

11:52.811 --> 11:53.941
Why?

11:54.021 --> 11:57.771
Floki is hiding too many secrets.

11:58.281 --> 12:00.821
He's lying about the execution order for Thors.

12:00.901 --> 12:02.701
I'm almost certain of it.

12:02.781 --> 12:03.611
Then why...?

12:04.951 --> 12:06.701
It's an assassination.

12:07.031 --> 12:10.871
Maybe it's a personal grudge or something.
But I'm sure he cooked this up all on his own.

12:10.951 --> 12:13.001
Who cares?

12:13.541 --> 12:16.461
It doesn't change the fact
that you'll get paid for killing him.

12:16.921 --> 12:19.881
Why do you think he didn't use one of his own men?

12:21.341 --> 12:24.221
Because that'd be going against orders.
He'd get his hands dirty.

12:24.301 --> 12:26.801
Well, that could be true.

12:27.971 --> 12:31.101
What if he's afraid of a loss?

12:31.601 --> 12:35.691
A loss so large that he won't
be able to explain it to his boss.

12:36.611 --> 12:39.361
An entire Jomsvikings unit?

12:39.441 --> 12:42.901
Just to get one washed-up soldier? That's crazy.

12:46.111 --> 12:48.911
Hey. Come down from there, kid.

12:51.291 --> 12:53.791
I want to get a look at this guy.

12:53.871 --> 12:55.461
"The Troll of Jom."

12:56.671 --> 13:00.381
I hope he's a fun guy.

13:19.561 --> 13:22.781
I can't even see the stars. I can't see anything.

13:22.861 --> 13:25.111
Which way are we heading?

13:26.201 --> 13:27.361
Thors.

13:27.741 --> 13:30.371
The wind changed a bit. Slightly to the right.

13:31.031 --> 13:33.661
I'll lead. Follow me.

13:33.751 --> 13:34.751
Got it.

13:41.961 --> 13:43.631
Amazing.

13:44.211 --> 13:48.131
How can Leif sail through the sea like this
without getting lost?

13:55.231 --> 13:56.101
Ari.

13:57.141 --> 13:59.151
Don't stare into the sea at night.

13:59.901 --> 14:01.401
It'll pull you in.

14:08.071 --> 14:09.661
Hey, Thors.

14:10.821 --> 14:13.161
What is it like on the battlefield?

14:15.041 --> 14:17.751
I heard you fought in a lot of battles.

14:18.541 --> 14:20.791
Tell us some stories.

14:21.671 --> 14:23.671
I want to cut off some general's head,

14:23.751 --> 14:25.171
so I can become a real man too.

14:29.051 --> 14:30.181
I see.

14:30.841 --> 14:34.181
My daughter likes strong men.

14:34.261 --> 14:35.931
You have a tough job ahead.

14:36.021 --> 14:38.891
Well, what can I say?

14:38.981 --> 14:40.191
You can tell?

14:41.351 --> 14:43.191
Are you in love with Ylva, Ari?

14:43.271 --> 14:46.191
Yeah, I like her. She's cute.

14:48.361 --> 14:52.991
She was born while I was still
in the Jomsvikings army.

14:53.531 --> 14:55.581
She was my first child.

15:04.921 --> 15:06.551
You're so loud.

15:06.631 --> 15:09.921
Do all babies cry so much?

15:10.011 --> 15:13.851
-Thors. Don't hold her like that.
-Her neck. Support her neck.

15:16.011 --> 15:18.351
Give me a boy next, Helga.

15:19.271 --> 15:21.351
The leader wants a boy.

15:22.401 --> 15:25.771
My wife Helga is the daughter of the leader
of the army.

15:26.821 --> 15:30.241
It was a difficult birth. She looked pale.

15:30.901 --> 15:31.911
Thors.

15:33.741 --> 15:35.621
Give her a name.

15:36.201 --> 15:37.621
Name her as you see fit.

15:38.201 --> 15:39.451
I'm busy.

15:39.871 --> 15:41.671
We're about to go on a campaign to Norway.

15:42.171 --> 15:44.131
Thors, the ship will soon depart.

15:44.211 --> 15:45.881
Okay. I'm coming.

15:45.961 --> 15:46.961
Thors.

15:51.171 --> 15:53.591
Give this child a name.

15:55.101 --> 15:57.561
I've been with her for 15 years,

15:58.011 --> 15:59.471
but that's the only time

15:59.721 --> 16:01.181
I've ever seen Helga mad.

16:07.151 --> 16:10.361
Ylva was my mother's name.

16:11.071 --> 16:12.861
It came to me all of a sudden.

16:13.861 --> 16:17.121
Now that I think about it, that's when it started.

16:18.621 --> 16:21.961
That's when I started to get scared of battle.

16:25.041 --> 16:26.631
That's why I ran away.

16:28.751 --> 16:33.011
I bet my old war buddies would curse me
if they knew.

16:36.761 --> 16:40.011
Hey. I can see the Faroe Islands.

16:58.531 --> 17:00.791
Father. Father.

17:00.871 --> 17:04.291
Are we in England? Did we arrive in England?

17:04.751 --> 17:07.041
No. Wrong answer.

17:07.501 --> 17:09.291
These are the Faroe Islands.

17:09.381 --> 17:12.341
They're in the middle, between Iceland and Norway.

17:12.421 --> 17:15.301
Our journey will be easier if we rest here for a bit.

17:15.801 --> 17:18.301
There's a village beyond this cove.

17:18.851 --> 17:21.971
Let's get some water there.
And we can trade too.

17:23.731 --> 17:26.901
Are you planning to come along,
all the way to England?

17:26.981 --> 17:27.811
Yeah.

17:29.271 --> 17:30.731
Get ready to row.

17:38.871 --> 17:40.331
Come on, hang in there.

17:42.621 --> 17:44.661
I wish we didn't have to do this.

17:44.751 --> 17:45.831
My butt hurts.

17:56.011 --> 17:57.971
What's wrong, Leif?

17:58.051 --> 17:59.221
Something's wrong.

17:59.721 --> 18:00.601
What's wrong?

18:01.141 --> 18:03.221
I wonder what's wrong.

18:04.181 --> 18:06.981
Something feels different
from the last time I was here.

18:16.361 --> 18:18.151
I see. It's the number of houses.

18:18.661 --> 18:20.491
The number of houses decreased.

18:21.531 --> 18:24.541
Let's turn back, Leif. I have a bad feeling about this.

18:24.991 --> 18:26.041
The terrain's bad too.

18:26.121 --> 18:28.161
What? Are you serious?

18:32.671 --> 18:35.591
Hey. They're going backwards.

18:35.671 --> 18:36.551
Did they notice us?

18:37.011 --> 18:38.381
They're good.

18:38.471 --> 18:41.051
They're very careful. They might be strong.

18:41.391 --> 18:43.761
They're too close, but it can't be helped.

18:43.851 --> 18:46.561
I don't care if the ships get damaged. Do it.

19:19.881 --> 19:21.591
Our exit...

19:22.681 --> 19:23.801
Take that.

19:23.891 --> 19:27.681
Great. They're caught like rats in a trap.

19:28.431 --> 19:31.191
Thors. Everyone. Are you okay?

19:31.271 --> 19:32.101
Is everyone okay?

19:32.521 --> 19:34.611
-Yes.
-We're okay.

19:35.151 --> 19:37.481
They will fire arrows.
Cover your head with your shield.

19:38.481 --> 19:40.321
Leif. How's the damage over there?

19:40.401 --> 19:42.991
We're okay. The ship is fine and everyone is okay.

19:47.291 --> 19:48.241
They're coming.

19:49.121 --> 19:52.461
Whoever's behind this trap
is in the back of the cove.

19:52.541 --> 19:53.501
The back?

20:09.271 --> 20:10.351
Pirates?

20:20.691 --> 20:22.901
These pillars are from a house.

20:22.991 --> 20:25.491
We're completely blocked.

20:25.571 --> 20:27.031
They got us.

20:27.121 --> 20:30.331
Maybe they'll spare our lives if we surrender.

20:30.411 --> 20:31.661
How do you know?

20:31.751 --> 20:33.081
They won't spare our lives.

20:33.161 --> 20:37.291
If they catch us, they'll sell us at the slave market.
Get ready.

20:37.381 --> 20:41.171
This is nothing.

20:42.511 --> 20:44.091
There's only two ships.

20:44.181 --> 20:45.431
Stop, Ari.

20:46.091 --> 20:47.551
They're experienced.

20:47.641 --> 20:51.431
They're not just some farmers working as pirates
in the summer for some extra cash.

20:51.721 --> 20:54.191
You're no match for them.

20:54.271 --> 20:56.481
Father...

21:08.241 --> 21:09.281
Thors...

21:22.421 --> 21:23.261
Thorfinn.

21:26.381 --> 21:29.891
Use it only to protect yourself. Understand?

21:29.971 --> 21:31.681
Only when you really need it.

21:39.481 --> 21:42.861
Are you going to kill them?
You are going to kill them.

21:44.901 --> 21:47.031
All right. I'm going to kill them.

21:47.111 --> 21:49.121
Stop saying "kill" so lightly.

21:56.461 --> 21:58.251
Bjorn. That mushroom...

21:59.251 --> 22:02.251
One, two, three...

22:02.341 --> 22:06.261
11, 12... And one kid?

22:06.761 --> 22:09.261
What? Is that all?

22:09.551 --> 22:11.721
Hey. Askeladd.

22:13.681 --> 22:16.141
Is it okay if I take care of them?

22:16.231 --> 22:19.191
It wouldn't be fun if all of us went after them at once.

22:19.271 --> 22:23.361
I'll go see
how good the Troll of Jom really is.

22:24.571 --> 22:27.531
Okay. They look like they want a fight too.

22:27.611 --> 22:28.451
What?

22:34.121 --> 22:36.411
-What?
-You bastard.

22:36.751 --> 22:38.291
What's wrong with you?

22:38.661 --> 22:40.751
Where did you come from?

22:44.381 --> 22:45.211
Brother.

22:46.631 --> 22:47.721
He's good.

22:47.921 --> 22:49.221
Take this.

23:06.111 --> 23:07.491
You're good...

23:09.241 --> 23:11.071
Troll of Jom.
